<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eógan mac Néill</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 465 (traditional)</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eógan mac Néill is the traditional ancestor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-neogain">Cenél nEógain</a>, one of the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niall-of-the-nine-hostages">Niall of the Nine Hostages</a> in Irish genealogy, said to have died in 465. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tir-eoghain">Tír Eoghain</a>, Eógan's land, now Tyrone, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inishowen">Inishowen</a> were named after him. The O'Neill and Mac Lochlainn kings of the north traced their descent from him.</p></div>
